export const title = "Avigilon ACC Integration Guide";
export const html = "<h1>Avigilon ACC Integration Guide</h1>\n      <hr class=\"rule\" />\n\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.1 Prerequisites</h3>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>AIBridge FW version 103000 or greater.</li>\n<li>Avigilon ACC 7.14 or greater.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">1.2 Understanding the Integration Architecture</h3>\n<p>There are two ways to integrate AIBridge with Avigilon ACC VMS:</p>\n\n<p><strong>1) Case 1</strong></p>\n<p>AIBridge receives the RTSP video stream from the IP camera, performs AI analysis, and provides an annotated video stream along with event data. The video is transcoded to include object recognition data, bounding boxes, and zone information.</p>\n\n<div class=\"figure\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 800 260\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;height:auto;font-family:-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <text x=\"30\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"24\">&#128247;</text>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <line x1=\"60\" y1=\"135\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"135\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"45\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"125\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#5b6270\">RTSP Video Stream</text>\n  <rect x=\"600\" y=\"30\" width=\"150\" height=\"90\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f2f3f6\" stroke=\"#9aa0ac\"/>\n  <text x=\"675\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#3a3f4a\" font-weight=\"700\">avigilon ACC7</text>\n  <rect x=\"600\" y=\"170\" width=\"130\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#0b0f19\"/>\n  <text x=\"665\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#fff\">AI Bridge</text>\n  <line x1=\"335\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"590\" y2=\"70\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arrv)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"675\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"665\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#e0a94c\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" marker-end=\"url(#arrv)\" marker-start=\"url(#arrv)\"/>\n  <text x=\"700\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#7a4f10\">AI Event &amp;<tspan x=\"700\" dy=\"14\">Annotated Video</tspan></text>\n  <line x1=\"335\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"590\" y2=\"215\" stroke=\"#8a8f9c\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" marker-end=\"url(#arrv)\"/>\n  <defs><marker id=\"arrv\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"6\" refY=\"3\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z\" fill=\"#8a8f9c\"/></marker></defs>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Case 1 &mdash; AIBridge receives RTSP from IP cameras and sends AI events &amp; annotated video to ACC</figcaption>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong>2) Case 2</strong></p>\n<p>Both AIBridge and Avigilon ACC VMS receive the RTSP video stream from the IP camera at the same time, and AIBridge sends only the AI analysis events to Avigilon ACC VMS. Instead of the IP camera's RTSP stream, AIBridge can also receive the RTSP stream from Avigilon ACC VMS.</p>\n\n<h2>2. Configuration</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.1 Avigilon ACC VMS Configuration</h3>\n<p>This document explains how to integrate AIBridge with Avigilon ACC VMS using the Case 1 method.</p>\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Install the ACC Web Endpoint service</strong><br>\nThe ACC Web Endpoint service must be installed on the same system as the ACC server software. Download and install the ACC 7 Web Endpoint service from the Avigilon website: <a href=\"https://www.avigilon.com/software-downloads\">https://www.avigilon.com/software-downloads</a>. Once installed, you can check the status of the ACC 7 Web Endpoint service at <code>https://localhost:8443/</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Add an 'api' account to Avigilon ACC VMS</strong><br>\nCreate an account for AIBridge to use when integrating with Avigilon ACC. This guide creates an account named <code>api</code>. From the Avigilon ACC client's site settings, click <strong>Users and Groups</strong>, then <strong>Add User</strong>. Enter <code>api</code> as the username, set the login timeout to 5 minutes, and select <strong>Password never expires</strong>. The created account needs permissions for alarm triggering and bookmark features &mdash; this guide selects Administrator rights.</li>\n<li><strong>Add AIBridge to Avigilon ACC VMS</strong><br>\nFrom the Avigilon ACC client, select <strong>Connect/Disconnect Devices</strong>. AIBridge behaves like an ONVIF device, so it is automatically detected by Avigilon ACC VMS. If it isn't detected automatically, check your network configuration. In each video channel's properties, click <strong>General</strong> to assign a Logical ID. This Logical ID is used to link channel information between AIBridge and Avigilon ACC, so make sure it doesn't overlap with other channels. The Logical ID assigned to each channel can be checked from the <strong>Site Health</strong> menu.</li>\n<li><strong>Add an AI alarm definition</strong><br>\nFrom the General panel of the Avigilon ACC client, select <strong>Alarms</strong>. Choose <strong>External Software Event</strong> as the trigger source, then select the video channel to integrate with this alarm. Enter <code>AI Event1</code> as the event name &mdash; this value is the required key that distinguishes events between AIBridge and Avigilon ACC, and must be entered in the \"Alarm ID\" field of AIBridge's Avigilon action handler settings. To use a different alarm per AIBridge channel, assign a video channel for each channel and create alarms sequentially as shown in the example.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">2.2 AIBridge Configuration</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Add a video stream</strong><br>\nConfigure (add) a video stream. You can add a video stream using ONVIF device discovery, or by directly adding the IP camera's RTSP stream address.</li>\n<li><strong>Configure the AI app</strong><br>\nSelect the AI app you want and configure the AI events for that channel. AIBridge provides over 50 AI applications for various use cases &mdash; see the full app list at the <a href=\"https://indoai.com/goods/catalog?page=1&searchMode=catalog&category=c0006&per=40&sorting=ranking&filter_display=lattice&code=0006\">catalog link</a>. Click the Add button in Actions Setting to add an Avigilon action handler.</li>\n<li><strong>Enter Avigilon ACC VMS server information</strong><br>\nEnter the Avigilon ACC VMS's IP address and other server information, then click the channel <strong>Mapping</strong> button. Enter the Camera Logical ID from Avigilon ACC VMS.\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;margin-top:14px;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">If the IP camera's Logical ID is entered instead of AIBridge's Logical ID in the camera mapping information, the integration works as Case 2.</p>\n</div>\nEnter the name of the Avigilon ACC \"Alarm\" you added earlier into the <strong>Alarm ID</strong> field &mdash; this guide uses <code>AI Event</code>. If you select <strong>Add Channel Number</strong>, the channel number is automatically appended to the Alarm ID (e.g. Channel 1: AI Event1, Channel 2: AI Event2, Channel 8: AI Event8). The Bookmark Message field can be used to send various additional information such as event text and LPR data.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"max-width:340px;\">\n<div class=\"app-panel\">\n  <div class=\"form-grid\" style=\"grid-template-columns:80px 1fr;\">\n    <span>Action Type</span><select disabled><option>Avigilon ACC</option></select>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"figure\" style=\"border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#fafbfc;\">\n<p style=\"margin:0;\">To set different Object properties for each AI app, you can create a separate Avigilon action handler for each AI app.</p>\n</div>\n\n<p>Click the Test button to check the test event in the Avigilon ACC client. If the test fails, check the error message shown in the top-right corner (e.g. VMS connection failure, authentication failure, invalid Alarm ID, invalid video Logical ID). If the test succeeds, check <strong>Activate Avigilon action handler</strong> and click <strong>Apply</strong> to save the handler settings. Finally, click <strong>Submit</strong> at the bottom of the AI app settings to save all configuration.</p>\n\n<h2>3. Demo</h2>\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.1 Live / Recorded</h3>\n<p>In Avigilon ACC's live view, the annotated video provided by AIBridge lets you check object recognition information, with a pink bounding box appearing when an event occurs. In Avigilon ACC's recorded data view, a bookmark icon appears on the timeline when an AI event occurs &mdash; clicking that bookmark shows the event's details.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.2 Search</h3>\n<p>From the bookmark search screen, you can search for AI events that were automatically bookmarked when they occurred. The Bookmark Message field in AIBridge's Avigilon settings can be used to dynamically generate various information &mdash; for example, using an LPR (License Plate Recognition) information template lets you find license plate information through bookmark search.</p>\n\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:24px;\">3.3 Alarm Manager</h3>\n<p>Clicking an individual alarm in the Alarm Manager shows the detailed event occurrence information along with the recorded video.</p>\n\n<h2>4. Revision History</h2>\n<ul class=\"steps\">\n<li>v1.00 Initial document creation.</li>\n</ul>";
